---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { wanderAppStoreUrl, wanderWebsiteUrl } from '../../lib/site-links';
import '../../styles/editorial.css';
import '../../styles/work.css';

/**
 * Every capability listed here was checked against the Cornerstone source on
 * 16 Sept 2026. Several claims from the old consulting site were removed or
 * corrected: QuickBooks is a push integration, not two-way sync; the backend is
 * Flask; there are seven modules, not sixteen; social posting is copy-paste
 * until Meta approves the app; the dollar and hours figures had no source.
 * Wander is a client project published under Daniel's own developer account,
 * which is why the App Store lists him as the seller. Its source was not
 * available to check, so its list is kept to what is publicly verifiable. Re-check before adding claims.
 */
const cornerstoneBuilt = [
  'Family and client records, with at-need and preneed arrangements',
  'A family portal for documents, arrangement status, estimates and messages',
  'A custom public website managed from the platform, including obituaries',
  'Documents generated from templates in Word, Excel and PDF',
  'Estimating and pricing',
  'AI reading of vendor invoices, with staff approval',
  'QuickBooks integration for customers, invoices and deposits',
  'Staff time tracking for payroll',
  'Marketing tools that apply the firm’s brand voice to every AI-assisted draft',
  'Grief support, anniversary and preneed email programs',
  'Community Partners Network: Support the Family',
  'SEO audits, Search Console and Google review data',
  'Campaign report cards at 30, 60 and 90 days',
  'A daily queue of marketing drafts waiting for approval',
  'One database underneath all of it',
];
const wanderBuilt = [
  'A native iPhone app, live on the App Store',
  'Park, playground and trail discovery for families',
  'Details that matter when you arrive, with photos and reviews',
  'Outing plans to share with friends',
  'The public website at wanderapp.ca',
  'App Store launch and release assets',
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Work" description="Software built by Hyphos Inc.: connected business software for Cornerstone Funeral Home, and Wander, a family app for finding parks and trails.">
<section class="product-editorial-hero page-shell"><p class="section-label">Selected Work</p><h1>Software We've<br />Shipped</h1><p>A small portfolio, by design. We take on a few engagements a year so we can stay close to the work. Two we can talk about publicly are below.</p><nav class="work-jump" aria-label="Jump to a project"><a href="#cornerstone">Connected Business Software <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a href="#wander">Wander <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></nav></section>

<section id="cornerstone" class="work-case page-shell">
  <div class="work-tags"><span class="work-tag">Business Software · Web</span><span class="work-status">In production</span></div>
  <h2>Connected Business Software</h2>
  <p class="work-lede">Client: Cornerstone Funeral Home. One platform for a relationship-driven business that had outgrown the standard industry stack.</p>
  <div class="work-links"><a href="/work/cornerstone" class="text-link">Take A Tour Of The Connected System <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="https://cornerstonefuneralhome.com" class="text-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit cornerstonefuneralhome.com <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>

  <div class="work-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="work-block"><p class="section-label">Client Brief</p><p>Replace a website nobody could update, marketing spend nobody could measure, family communication living in inboxes, and scheduling and intake on paper, with one system the staff could actually run. Respect the dignity of what a funeral home does: nothing generic, nothing that felt like off-the-shelf software.</p></div>
      <div class="work-block"><p class="section-label">What We Built</p><ul class="work-list">{cornerstoneBuilt.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul></div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="work-panel"><p class="section-label">What We Like About It</p><p>A funeral home is the kind of business where the relationship is the product. The software's job is to take the busywork off the staff so they can be present with families.</p><p>That constraint shaped the design: no notifications fighting for attention, no engagement loops, no dashboards that don't earn their place. Drafts wait for a person to approve them.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <figure class="work-figure">
    <div class="work-figure-head"><div><p class="section-label">A Look At The System</p><h3>The Staff Portal</h3></div><p>The internal modules belong to the client and aren't shown. The public site is at <a class="text-link" href="https://cornerstonefuneralhome.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cornerstonefuneralhome.com</a>.</p></div>
    <div class="work-shot"><img src="/work/cornerstone/staff-portal.png" width="2912" height="2340" alt="Cornerstone staff portal, calendar view" loading="lazy" /></div>
    <figcaption class="work-caption">Actual client software · Staff portal, calendar view</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="work-stack"><strong>Stack</strong><span>Python · Flask</span><span>Postgres</span><span>React · Astro</span><span>Anthropic · OpenAI</span><span>QuickBooks API</span><span>Search Console</span><span>Cloudflare</span></div>
</section>

<section id="wander" class="work-case page-shell">
  <div class="work-tags"><span class="work-tag">Client Project · iOS</span><span class="work-status">Available on the App Store</span></div>
  <h2>Wander</h2>
  <p class="work-lede">Client: Wander. A field guide for families: finding parks, playgrounds, trails and outdoor spots nearby, and getting out the door.</p>
  <div class="work-links"><a href={wanderAppStoreUrl} class="text-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Download On The App Store <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href={wanderWebsiteUrl} class="text-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit wanderapp.ca <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>

  <div class="work-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="work-block"><p class="section-label">The Brief</p><p>Take a family from "we should do something" to actually out the door, without a fifteen-minute planning session. Trustworthy information and the small details that matter when you arrive.</p></div>
      <div class="work-block"><p class="section-label">What We Built</p><ul class="work-list">{wanderBuilt.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul></div>
      <div class="work-block"><p class="section-label">Status</p><p>Live on the App Store and free to download on iPhone. Android is coming soon.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="work-panel"><p class="section-label">What We Like About It</p><p>Wander exists to get families outside, not to keep them in an app. Every screen has to earn its place.</p><p>That restraint is hard to keep while shipping. It only happens when it's a deliberate design choice from the first day, and it's the kind of constraint we like working under.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <figure class="work-figure">
    <div class="work-figure-head"><div><p class="section-label">A Look Inside The App</p><h3>Wander On iPhone</h3></div><p>Explore the map, check the details and make plans.</p></div>
    <div class="work-shots">
      <img src="/work/wander/wander-find.webp" width="640" height="1388" alt="Wander map showing nearby parks and playgrounds" loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/work/wander/wander-check.webp" width="640" height="1388" alt="Wander park details with photos, reviews and amenities" loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/work/wander/wander-go.webp" width="640" height="1388" alt="Wander outing plan to share with friends" loading="lazy" />
    </div>
  </figure>
</section>

<section class="product-editorial-closing page-shell"><span class="section-label">Other Engagements</span><h2>Most Of Our Work Doesn't<br />Have A Public Face</h2><p>Internal systems, back-office integrations and AI tooling for operations teams. If you'd like to hear about work relevant to your situation, ask.</p><a href="/contact" class="button button--gold">Ask About Relevant Work <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
</BaseLayout>
